# Supply-chain policy: only package versions released at least three weeks ago, pinned exactly.
# `before` makes npm ignore anything published after this date, transitive dependencies included
# (like `exclude-newer` in ../pyproject.toml). Move it forward deliberately, never to within three weeks.
# A version that fixes an open CVE is exempt: move the date just past its release, and note it here.
# Current exception, approved 2026-10-22: 2026-10-15 for next 16.4.1 (released 2026-10-14), which fixes
# GHSA-2464-fhr4-w9xw (unauthenticated RCE in the image optimizer) and GHSA-p3m5-59mp-jv5r (Server
# Actions DoS). It meets the rule again from 2026-11-05.
before=2026-10-15T00:00:00Z
save-exact=true
